  "worked_solution": "We start by solving $3w-7\\le 5:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3w-7 & \\le 5 \\\\ 3w & \\le 12 \\\\ w & \\le 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252742/assets/dfbf9fce10352e640bb62b75c49339e54c3d22b918e2dfb60a72472ef5129639.png)\n\nThen, we solve $5w+7\\ge -3:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5w+7 & \\ge -3 \\\\ 5w & \\ge -10 \\\\ w & \\ge -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252742/assets/535934975bf21706e8bfa3b54fa51a0f344f585e89f3003ad042f6fb660c3441.png)\n\nFinally, we solve $2w<8:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2w & <8 \\\\ w & <4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252742/assets/ba806ca20f496c724c4411c282ab44d81d7713c7b8635b3c286faff1d7728f20.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $w$ that satisfy at least one of the inequalities, we overlay the three graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252742/assets/f084c11e4faf4fdcfc69a32900bf62c1bddfa2266007f8f4ddecf8ab928230fa.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $-\\infty <w<\\infty .$",
